<article class="env-lemma" id="0H3Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H3Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0H3Q">29.56.7</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has finitely many irreducible components. Let $\nu : X^\nu \to X$ be the normalization of $X$. Then the seminormalization of $X$ in $X^\nu $ is is the seminormalization of $X$. In a formula: $X^{sn} = X^{X^\nu /sn}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : Y \to X$ be as in (<a href="/tag/035M" data-tag="035M">29.55.0.1</a>) so that $X^\nu $ is the normalization of $X$ in $Y$. The seminormalization $X^{sn} \to X$ of $X$ is the initial object in the category of universal homeomorphisms $X' \to X$ inducing isomorphisms on residue fields. Since $Y$ is the disjoint union of the spectra of the residue fields at the generic points of irreducible components of $X$, we see that for any $X' \to X$ in this category we obtain a canonical lift $f' : Y \to X'$ of $f$. Then by Lemma <a href="/tag/035I" data-tag="035I">29.54.4</a> we obtain a canonical morphism $X^\nu \to X'$. Whence in turn a canonical morphism $X^{X^\nu /sn} \to X'$ by the universal property of $X^{X^\nu /sn}$. In this way we see that $X^{X^\nu /sn}$ satisfies the same universal property that $X^{sn}$ has and we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>